      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Fragile API Change: Pointer Casting to Opaque Struct\nThe patch changes the signature of `egis_finger_match` and `egis_finger_enroll` to accept `FP_EGIS_IMAGE *` instead of `uint8_t *`.\n\n- Issue: In `egis_private.c` and `egis_egis630_bio_alg.c`, the code casts the raw image buffer `(a uint8_t *)` directly to `FP_EGIS_IMAGE *`.\n\n- Risk: Unless `FP_EGIS_IMAGE` is specifically designed to be a transparent alias for a byte array starting at the same address, this is a strict aliasing violation. If `FP_EGIS_IMAGE` is a struct with specific members, passing a raw buffer not aligned or structured correctly will cause undefined behavior or crashes.\n\nRecommendation: Verify the definition of `FP_EGIS_IMAGE`. If it is a structured object, the buffer should be wrapped or initialized properly rather than force-cast.",
